{"chunk_id": "fe9720f08dc1", "text": "After Sita\u2019s abduction, Rama wanders the forest in mounting grief and desperation. He sends Lakshmana to search the sacred Godaveri River, but Sita is nowhere to be found; even the river and forest spirits remain silent out of fear of Ravana. Questioning animals and the landscape itself, Rama receives a strange clue when deer gesture toward the south, hinting at the path of the abductor. Soon the brothers discover scattered flowers Sita had worn, broken weapons, shattered chariot parts, blood, and footprints of both Sita and a mighty titan, revealing a violent struggle. Believing demons may have killed or devoured her, Rama\u2019s sorrow transforms into cosmic fury. He vows to unleash his divine power and, if the gods do not return Sita, threatens to destroy the Three Worlds themselves\u2014revealing the terrifying scale of his latent divinity.\nGrief-stricken Rama searches for Sita, discovers signs of her abduction, and in furious despair vows to destroy the worlds if she is not returned.\nThemes: grief and loss, righteous wrath, search for Sita, omens and traces, cosmic threat", "vector": [0.009125323966145515, -0.022257857024669647, -0.0004885024391114712, -0.0012547321384772658, -0.0225752592086792, 0.023342315107584, -0.04073333367705345, -0.016465259715914726, -0.018515150994062424, -0.022376881912350655, 0.00447008665651083, 0.014626969583332539, 0.009079036302864552, 0.011565356515347958, 0.012881254777312279, 0.018964804708957672, 0.04639367759227753, -0.001666363561525941, 0.04628787934780121, -0.012167098931968212, 0.005180935841053724, -0.0064736902713775635, -0.002230083802714944, 0.0004632920608855784, -0.01946735940873623, -0.015711428597569466, 0.02223140560090542, -0.04353705421090126, 0.024770626798272133, -0.010150270536541939, -0.023448117077350616, -0.016121406108140945, -0.014693094417452812, -0.01597592979669571, -0.011605031788349152, 0.01261014025658369, 0.009932056069374084, -0.013522672466933727, 